764	775	757	759	my ancient captain	54	“ He who strikes first oft - times strikes last . ”
901	906	907	907	he	11	“ Thou careful man ! ”
918	942	907	907	he	11	“ Who else , think you , in this or any other hundred , now bars his gate when the sun goes down ? ”
943	950	951	951	I	0	“ It is my sunset gun , ”
1007	1014	1015	1015	he	11	“ Of what were you dreaming ? ”
1031	1037	1015	1015	he	11	“ I called you twice . ”
1038	1051	1052	1052	He	11	“ I was wishing for Dale 's times and Dale 's laws . ”
1080	1085	1086	1086	he	11	“ Thou Mars incarnate ! ”
1089	1131	1086	1086	he	11	“ Thou first , last , and in the meantime soldier ! Why , what wilt thou do when thou gettest to heaven ? Make it too hot to hold thee ? Or take out letters of marque against the Enemy ? ”
1132	1139	1140	1140	I	0	“ I am not there yet , ”
1144	1158	1140	1140	I	0	“ In the meantime I would like a commission against -- your relatives . ”
1187	1195	1196	1196	I	0	“ I would your princess were alive , ”
1200	1205	1206	1206	he	11	“ So do I , ”
1210	1214	1222	1222	he	11	“ So do I. ”
1232	1239	1240	1240	he	11	“ Brave and wise and gentle , ”
1243	1273	1240	1240	he	11	“ If I did not think to meet her again , beyond that star , I could not smile and speak calmly , Ralph , as I do now . ”
1274	1282	1283	1283	I	0	“ ' T is a strange thing , ”
1292	1355	1283	1283	I	0	“ Love for your brother - in - arms , love for your commander if he be a commander worth having , love for your horse and dog , I understand . But wedded love ! to tie a burden around one 's neck because ' t is pink and white , or clear bronze , and shaped with elegance ! Faugh ! ”
1356	1372	1373	1373	he	11	“ Yet I came with half a mind to persuade thee to that very burden ! ”
1380	1386	1387	1387	I	0	“ Thanks for thy pains , ”
1397	1407	1408	1408	he	11	“ I have ridden to - day from Jamestown , ”
1412	1488	1408	1408	he	11	“ I was the only man , i ' faith , that cared to leave its gates ; and I met the world -- the bachelor world -- flocking to them . Not a mile of the way but I encountered Tom , Dick , and Harry , dressed in their Sunday bravery and making full tilt for the city . And the boats upon the river ! I have seen the Thames less crowded . ”
1489	1497	1498	1498	I	0	“ There was more passing than usual , ”
1501	1520	1498	1498	I	0	“ but I was busy in the fields , and did not attend . What 's the lodestar ? ”
1521	1538	1408	1408	he	11	“ The star that draws us all,--some to ruin , some to bliss ineffable , woman . ”
1539	1549	1498	1498	I	0	“ Humph ! The maids have come , then ? ”
1553	1567	1550	1550	He	0	“ There 's a goodly ship down there , with a goodly lading . ”
1568	1585	1586	1586	I	0	“ Videlicet , some fourscore waiting damsels and milkmaids , warranted honest by my Lord Warwick , ”
1589	1606	1607	1607	he	0	“ This business hath been of Edwyn Sandys ' management , as you very well know , ”
1614	1641	1607	1607	he	0	“ His word is good : therefore I hold them chaste . That they are fair I can testify , having seen them leave the ship . ”
1642	1647	1648	1648	I	0	“ Fair and chaste , ”
1651	1656	1648	1648	I	0	“ but meanly born . ”
1657	1663	1664	1664	he	0	“ I grant you that , ”
1667	1865	1664	1664	he	0	“ But after all , what of it ? Beggars must not be choosers . The land is new and must be peopled , nor will those who come after us look too curiously into the lineage of those to whom a nation owes its birth . What we in these plantations need is a loosening of the bonds which tie us to home , to England , and a tightening of those which bind us to this land in which we have cast our lot . We put our hand to the plough , but we turn our heads and look to our Egypt and its fleshpots . ' T is children and wife -- be that wife princess or peasant -- that make home of a desert , that bind a man with chains of gold to the country where they abide . Wherefore , when at midday I met good Master Wickham rowing down from Henricus to Jamestown , to offer his aid to Master Bucke in his press of business to - morrow , I gave the good man Godspeed , and thought his a fruitful errand and one pleasing to the Lord . ”
1866	1869	1870	1870	I	0	“ Amen , ”
1873	1889	1870	1870	I	0	“ I love the land , and call it home . My withers are unwrung . ”
1932	1935	1936	1936	he	0	“ Ralph , ”
1947	1964	1936	1936	he	0	“ have you ever an hundred and twenty pounds of tobacco in hand ? If not , I”--
1965	1971	1972	1972	I	0	“ I have the weed , ”
1975	1979	1972	1972	I	0	“ What then ? ”
1980	2004	1936	1936	he	0	“ Then at dawn drop down with the tide to the city , and secure for thyself one of these same errant damsels . ”
